{"ts":"2026-07-11T22:54:55.183Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"GH-515 (open, filed 2026-07-11 against pm 2026.7.5, extension-free repro with isolated PM_PATH/PM_GLOBAL_PATH). Adding four tests via pm test <id> --add command=\"echo ONE|TWO|THREE|NEWEST\" yields stored order NEWEST,ONE,THREE,TWO — --add places the new command at index 1 while --only-last picks the tail, so 'run the test I just added' executes a stale command instead. Bite: agents add a temporary/safe command then --run --only-last and get an unintended older command (issue author hit a stale provider probe). Fix directions from the issue: (1) make --add append-stable, or (2) add --only-newest/--only-added-last and document that --only-last means last-in-stored-order. Prefer (1): append-stable storage is the least-surprise contract and keeps --only-last meaning both 'tail' and 'newest'."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-x2vx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-515: pm test --add reorders linked tests — --only-last can execute a non-newest command"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":""},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","gh-issue"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-11T22:54:55.183Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-11T22:54:55.183Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm test --add appends deterministically so the newly added test is the tail entry (or an explicit --only-newest selector is added and documented); regression spec reproduces the 4-add reorder from GH-515 (ONE/TWO/THREE/NEWEST) and asserts --only-last runs the just-added command; docs state the selector semantics explicitly"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bcfdd60d33be63ab16be3078cbf09f61c73a69b416cb77500be6ff9f7eebf914","message":""}
